+## Two-host EP16 through FlashInfer
+
+An EP world on two hosts of 2 x 4 GPUs runs `p2p_split` like EP8 on one host:
+GPUs are identified by (host, PCI bus), only the GPUs of one host and NUMA
+node are P2P peers, and each of the other 12 peers is a cross peer with its
+own shadow segment (13 segments per rank). The `ep16_2x2numa` anchor entries
+apply through the folded `ep_numa_split` view.
+
+Packed dispatch is on where the drop's heuristic selects it
+(`select_xnuma_pack`: EP16 from 32 rows per rank; `MEGAMOE_XNUMA_PACK=0|1`
+overrides it on every rank). The shim decides it per compile bucket at
+workspace allocation: a bucket packs only if its K1 uses the token-strided
+pull, and the shared control region contains the packed staging area as soon
+as one bucket packs. The sender is the standalone's, placed with the
+region's strides and addressed inside the owner's shadow segment: the packed
+activation rows go to the shadow of the activation buffer and
+`map | weights | scales` to the shadow of the scale buffer, which with the
+route-id and weight buffers behind it holds them for every bucket up to the
+workspace capacity.
